"""The official TxDOT logo, as vector artwork.

PROVENANCE -- this is the real mark, not a redrawing.
Extracted verbatim from the official TxDOT PowerPoint template:

    txdot-presentation-template.potx  ->  ppt/media/image3.svg

That is the horizontal lockup used in the header band of the TxDOT content slides
(swoosh-into-star + "Texas Department of Transportation" on one line). The .potx also
ships a stacked lockup at ppt/media/image1.svg (mark above a three-line wordmark) used
on cover slides and the poster -- pull that one from the template if a cover is ever added.

The only edits to the source artwork are non-visual:
  * fill="#FFFFFF" -> fill="currentColor" (36 paths) so the same asset works on the blue
    band and on a white surface; the header sets color:#fff
  * removed the PowerPoint-specific id="Layer_1", overflow="hidden" and the empty <defs>
  * added class/role/aria-label for the page

Do NOT hand-edit the path data. If the mark ever needs replacing, re-extract from the
current official template rather than adjusting these coordinates.
"""

